 ### Contextual emits
 
-We've upgraded the API of the `EventEmitter.on`, `EventEmitter.once` and
-`EventEmitter.removeListener` to accept an extra argument which is the `context`
+We've upgraded the API of the `EventEmitter.on`, `EventEmitter.once`,
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` and `EventEmitter.removeListener` to accept an extra
+argument which is the `context`
 or `this` value that should be set for the emitted events. This means you no
 longer have the overhead of an event that required `fn.bind` in order to get a
 custom `this` value.
@@ -72,6 +73,21 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `on`, but returns an idempotent
+function that cancels only that registration. This is useful when the caller
+owns a subscription lifecycle or when the same function and context are
+registered more than once. Unlike `off` and `removeListener`, cancellation
+does not remove other matching registrations.
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // Safe to call again.
+```
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
